(V)--(also शुरद्वत्) a sage by garbha;
1: वा. ५९. ९३.
heard the वायु पुराण from त्रिधामा and narrated it to त्रिविष्ठ;
2: Br. II. ३८. २८; III. ७४. ६०; IV. 4. ६१; वा. १०३. ६१.
see Gautama.

(I)--a sage by garbha of the सावर्णि epoch;
1: M. 9. ३२; वा. 1. १८६; ५९. ९३.
husband of अहल्या and father of शतानन्द;
2: M. ५०. 8; Vi. IV. १९. ६३.
a ऋषिक and a मन्त्रकृत्।
3: M. १४५. ९५, १०४.

--the pleasure garden of उमा and शिव in the हिमालयस्;
1: M. ११. ४४; वा. ४१. ३७.
here Ila was converted into a female;
2: M. १२. 1.
कुमार born in.
3: वा. ७२. ३२.

--a name of शिव Rudra;
1: भा. VI. १५. २८; Br. II. २५. २३; M. १८०. १९; Vi. I. 8. 6; १५. १२२; III. 2. ११; V. ३४. 1.
the presiding deity of the earth;
2: M. २६५. ४०.
represents the earth and hence the earth should not be made impure or unclean;
3: Br. II. १०. १०.
the lord created by ब्रह्मा in the ३०थ् Kalpa who made अट्टहास;
4: वा. २२. २८.
the third son of कृष्णलोहित;
5: Ib. २७. २८.
his wife, विकेशि and son अन्गारक.
6: Br. II. १०. ७८; १३. ५४.

--(महानदी) R. in भारतवर्ष; its source was visited by बलराम who then travelled to प्रयागा along its bank. The river of अयोध्या; Asamanjasa used to throw into it the children who were his playmates.
1: भा. V. १९. १८; IX. 8. १७; X. ७९. 9-१०; Br. III. १२. Ib. १५; III. ५१. ६५; ५५. ११; वा. १०८. ७९;
R. from the हिमालयस्;
2: Br. II. १६. २५.
sacred तीर्थ;
3: M. २२. १९.
one of the १६ rivers married by हव्यवाहन;
4: Ib. ५१. १४; वा. २९. १४.
in the Vaidyuta hill and has its source in the मानस lake;
5: Br. II. १८. १५ and ७०; M. ११४. २१; १२१. १७.
a राक्षस named ब्रह्मपाद lived in [page३-553+ ४७] the forest here called वैभ्राज्यम्;
6: वा. ४५. ९५; ४७. १५.
in the chariot of Tripu- रारि.
7: M. १३३. M; १६३. ६०.

(I)--(वाक् Devi1); विश्वरूपा, a mind-born daughter of ब्रह्मा who began to love her. Being criticised by his sons for it, he gave up his body in shame. Presented पृथु with a wreath, and was offered a wreath of pearls by विश्वकर्मन्. Gave away a string of beads to the Lord. Gave वीण to कुमार; a Mother goddess.
2: Br. III. १०. ४७; ३५. ४४. IV. 7. ७२; १९. ७०, ७३; २०. १०१; ३६. १९; ४०. 8;
The Goddess of Learning;
3: M. 1. 2;
enshrined in the faces of ब्रह्मा,
4: Ib. १३. ५२;
गायत्रा
5: Ib. २४६. ५७;
in the २३र्द् Kalpa; constitutes ३२ aks2aras; is प्रकृति and गौली,
6: वा. २३. ३८;
source of all worlds;
7: Ib. २३. ५४-5;
of four feet.
8: Ib. २३. ८८;
Presented to Skanda a great वीर.
9: Ib. ७२. ४५.
